# Simulation output. The nine demo runs already committed here stay tracked --
# .gitignore does not untrack existing files -- so a clone still ships worked
# examples that open with populated analytics and working exports. Everything a
# local run writes from now on is ignored: those are per-instance research data,
# often gigabytes, and nothing downstream should depend on them being in git.
logs/
logs.bak/


myreadme.*

# Redundant/development files (use README.md instead)
SIMULATION_BUILDER_README.md
Peace-Negotiation-Simulation-Readme.md
concordia_cheatsheet.md
negotiatepeace.py

# User-saved simulation configs (per-instance data)
backend/saved_configs/*.json

# Untracked documentation
blog_article.md
simulation_for_sdgs.md
GLM_SETUP.md
DIAGNOSTIC_IMPROVEMENTS.md
documentation.html

# Custom documentation (only track selected files)
docs/**
!docs/SIMULATION_TEMPLATES_GUIDE.md
!docs/SIMULATION_BUILDING_GUIDE.md
!docs/TIMEOUT_CONFIGURATION.md
!docs/TEMPLATE_CREATION_GUIDE.md
!docs/QUANTITATIVE_RESEARCH_FEATURES.md
!docs/research-use-cases/
docs/research-use-cases/*
!docs/research-use-cases/vaccine-hesitancy-study.md
!docs/research-use-cases/phishing-attack-simulation.md
!docs/research-use-cases/urban-gentrification-simulation.md

# Test scripts
test_glm.py
